Research: .collab/research/2026-10-16-t3-code-c2c-support.md and live receipt JSON. Quality: preserve existing codebase architecture; small typed interfaces; meaningful regression and failure tests; no mock-only delivery claims; no whole-tree refactor; independent review/fix loop before merge. Decisions and evidence must be appended through bl. Implement coherent T3 settings/CLI setup and c2c doctor/install integration as supported by finalized contract. Expose configured, pending, delivered, held/unsupported states without message bodies or credentials. Outbound sender derived from exact T3 thread. Document install/uninstall and supported providers; do not claim unverified adapters. Follow existing UI/config style.

Review decision: host mode must explicitly disable the native c2c MCP server in effective provider configuration; C2C_NO_AUTO_REGISTER and C2C_MCP_AUTO_DRAIN_CHANNEL alone do not remove a second manual consumer. Use a uniform server-level opt-in, sanitize inherited per-thread c2c identity, preserve native defaults when off, and verify tool inventory/attempt behavior. Inbox/status must bound payload output and allow explicit dismissal of held/unsupported records to recover capacity.